course: dictionary
lesson: 3627
title: Finders, keepers?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A finder is a person who finds something. The ending -er often means someone or something that does a job, as in a teacher or a runner. So find plus -er gives finder. «Children in the playground often shout "finders keepers, losers weepers", but a lost thing does not stop belonging to its owner just because you found it.» Here, the finder is the child who found the thing.
explain: A finder can also be a tool or device that helps you find something. A viewfinder shows you what a camera will photograph. A stud finder helps a builder locate hidden supports inside a wall. The context tells you which meaning is right: a finder that is a person is found in «the finder of the lost wallet», and a finder that is a tool is named in a phrase like «viewfinder».
explain: Context helps here too. «"Finders keepers" is not true for things like phones; keeping something you could return is a kind of stealing, and lost property offices exist to return things.» The sentence tells you that the saying is not a fair rule for valuable things. When you find something lost, take it to a grown-up, the school office, or the police.
explain: Words from other places can also be checked in context. «His mate says, "Finders keepers." But somewhere a kid is upset about losing it.» Here the words after "But" show that the saying does not match what really happens. A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: A finder is a person who finds something.
fact: A finder can also be a tool or device that helps you find something, such as a viewfinder on a camera.
fact: Finders keepers, losers weepers is a playground saying, not a fair rule for lost things.
fact: «Finders keepers» means what you find is yours, according to the saying.
fact: Lost property offices exist to return lost things to their owners.
fact: Phrases with finder include finder's fee, viewfinder, pathfinder and stud finder.
exercise: «The finder of the lost wallet handed it in at the school office.» What is a finder in this sentence? | A kind of football game | A bag for carrying books | A tool that cooks food | *A person who finds something
exercise: A camera has a viewfinder to help you line up a photo. What does a viewfinder do? | It makes the photo louder | It keeps the camera dry | *It helps you see and aim what you want to photograph
exercise: «Finders keepers» is a playground saying. Why is it not fair for a lost phone? | *Because a lost thing still belongs to its owner, and you could return it | Because phones are always found in the school hall | Because phones are too small to keep | Because it is only for summer
test: A stud finder helps a builder find what? | *Hidden supports inside a wall | Lost keys | Birds' nests | Fresh bread
test: Mam says the room is a tip. What does tip mean here? | Very quiet | Very cold | Very lovely | *Very messy
exam: «His mate says, "Finders keepers." But somewhere a kid is upset about losing it.» What does this tell you? | *Keeping a lost thing can upset its owner | The mate is angry with the kid | Keeping a lost thing is always fine | The kid found the thing and is happy
